# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Cloudflare reads this file from the ROOT OF THE BUILD OUTPUT, so it lives in
# public/ and Astro copies it to dist/ verbatim. It is not served as a file.
#
# ⚠️ EVERYTHING IN THIS FILE FOLLOWS THE SITE INTO PRODUCTION. That is the whole
# difference from netlify.toml, which sat at the repo root and was never copied
# into dist/ — so it could carry preview-only rules safely and this file cannot.
#
# So this file holds ONLY rules that are correct on the real procedoinfo.com as
# well as on the preview. The preview's `X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow` is NOT
# here, and must never be added here: it would follow the build into production
# and quietly de-index the real launch. It is appended to dist/_headers at
# deploy time by scripts/preview-headers.cjs, which `npm run build:preview`
# runs and `npm run build` does not.
#
# The same trap is why public/robots.txt carries no Disallow — see the note in
# that file.

# Added 2026-09-19 after auditing what the live site actually sent: nosniff and
# Referrer-Policy and nothing else. For a firm whose own services page sells
# Facilities Security and "Enterprise-Grade Security", a prospect who runs the
# site through securityheaders.com or Mozilla Observatory is a plausible
# visitor — and the grade was the kind you do not want them to see. The
# technical risk on a static brochure site with no auth and no user content is
# genuinely low; the credibility risk is not.
#
# Each of these denies something the site does not do, so none can break it:
#   HSTS                 the site is HTTPS-only already; this stops a first
#                        request being made over http. No `preload` — that is a
#                        one-way door for a domain and is Procedo's call, not a
#                        default to slip in.
#   X-Frame-Options      nothing should ever frame this site.
#   Permissions-Policy   no camera, microphone or geolocation is used anywhere.
#   COOP                 no cross-origin window is opened or talked to.
#
# STILL MISSING: Content-Security-Policy. It is not here because it cannot be
# written by hand — Astro inlines three module scripts plus the reveal
# bootstrap, so a strict policy needs their sha256 hashes, which change with
# every build. That needs a post-build step, and a wrong CSP breaks the site
# silently for visitors rather than loudly at build time. Worth doing, worth
# doing carefully, and deliberately not bundled in with the free wins above.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Astro fingerprints these filenames, so they can be cached forever.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
